WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.446 --> 00:00:07.571
- What?

00:00:17.603 --> 00:00:19.809
- [Voiceover] Lady's Brunch.

00:00:19.809 --> 00:00:21.222
- Oh, hell yeah.

00:00:21.222 --> 00:00:22.716
- Ladies eat this?

00:00:23.891 --> 00:00:25.967
- Who eats this thing?

00:00:25.967 --> 00:00:28.579
- So, it looks like it's
just a regular cheeseburger

00:00:28.579 --> 00:00:30.645
except there's egg, bacon, and of course,

00:00:30.645 --> 00:00:33.003
a Krispy Kreme as the bun.

00:00:33.003 --> 00:00:34.030
- Let's do this.

00:00:37.527 --> 00:00:37.825
- Whoa.

00:00:37.825 --> 00:00:39.811
- It tastes pretty much exactly how

00:00:39.811 --> 00:00:41.028
you think it would taste.

00:00:41.028 --> 00:00:42.467
- It's delicious.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:46.735
Is it an innovation on
a standard burger? No.

00:00:46.747 --> 00:00:48.217
- It looks like a peanut butter sandwich

00:00:48.217 --> 00:00:50.569
but there's white on it?

00:00:50.569 --> 00:00:52.557
- Is that Marshmallow Fluff?

00:00:52.557 --> 00:00:54.896
- This better not be
mayonnaise and peanut butter.

00:00:56.844 --> 00:00:59.612
- Whoa. That's not Marshmallow Fluff.

00:01:01.808 --> 00:01:03.322
- Is it mayonnaise?

00:01:04.741 --> 00:01:06.118
- That's mayonnaise and peanut butter.

00:01:06.118 --> 00:01:07.808
- This is mayonnaise?

00:01:07.808 --> 00:01:09.928
- It's actually good.

00:01:09.928 --> 00:01:12.291
- Better than I thought it would be.

00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:13.586
- [Voiceover] When you
first told me Scrapple,

00:01:13.586 --> 00:01:15.463
I thought it was going to be a drink.

00:01:15.463 --> 00:01:19.485
- It's like trimmings
and stuff. It's fried.

00:01:20.945 --> 00:01:22.355
- It smells like meat.

00:01:24.737 --> 00:01:25.939
It doesn't have a bad flavor

00:01:25.939 --> 00:01:28.777
but it has a really weird texture.

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:34.015
- Just to, it has a winning
formula for human food;

00:01:34.015 --> 00:01:37.390
fat, meat, put that on fire,

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.126
and you got delicious.

00:01:40.126 --> 00:01:42.176
- [Voiceover] So here, we have olive loaf.

00:01:42.176 --> 00:01:44.204
- This looks like a cartoon food.

00:01:44.204 --> 00:01:46.793
- It's the meat equivalent
of a fruitcake, right?

00:01:46.793 --> 00:01:49.045
- I mean, I don't know
why it's just olive.

00:01:49.045 --> 00:01:50.823
There should be other
things embedded in it,

00:01:50.823 --> 00:01:52.503
like even more meat.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:54.727
- Oh my God.

00:01:54.727 --> 00:01:56.445
- Nope. Definitely no.

00:01:58.506 --> 00:02:00.954
- Yeah, it's like really
salty, but I don't hate it.

00:02:00.954 --> 00:02:02.475
- I don't know when you would be like,

00:02:02.475 --> 00:02:04.100
"Oh, give me olive loaf," as opposed to,

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:06.016
"Give me ham, or give me Spam,

00:02:06.016 --> 00:02:08.152
or give me turkey or anything else."

00:02:08.152 --> 00:02:11.592
- Olive loaf. It's better than bologna.

00:02:11.592 --> 00:02:13.033
- [Voiceover] Oh, are
these Kool-Aid pickles?

00:02:13.033 --> 00:02:14.201
- What?

00:02:17.442 --> 00:02:18.496
- What the f-

00:02:18.496 --> 00:02:21.074
- I hate pickles but I love Kool-Aid.

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:23.048
- Just purely from an
aesthetic standpoint,

00:02:23.048 --> 00:02:24.344
this is beautiful.

00:02:27.485 --> 00:02:28.195
- Good.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:33.501
- I've never eaten like
a full pickle before,

00:02:33.501 --> 00:02:34.825
like I take one bite and spit it out,

00:02:34.825 --> 00:02:36.481
but I'm going to eat this whole pickle.

00:02:39.199 --> 00:02:41.962
I bit my tongue. F-

00:02:41.962 --> 00:02:43.154
- Better than a normal pickle?

00:02:46.151 --> 00:02:47.034
Yeah.

